	"data": "Concept: Atomic Notes\n\nWhat It Is\nThe design principle underlying the Calcifer Vault. Each note covers exactly one thing. Relationships are expressed as explicit [[wikilinks]]. Context is composed on demand by loading only relevant nodes.\n\nDerived from Zettelkasten methodology, adapted for agent memory.\n\nWhy It Matters\nMonolithic files degrade: they grow unbounded, load entirely into context, and bury fresh signal under stale noise. Atomic notes scale: as the corpus grows, context window cost…",
